    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nCharming two-bedroom detached cottage located in a peaceful countryside setting while still enjoying excellent connectivity to Kilkenny City and surrounding towns.\n\nThis delightful property offers comfortable living accommodation throughout and presents an ideal opportunity for first-time buyers, those seeking to downsize, or anyone looking for a countryside residence within easy reach of key amenities. The accommodation briefly comprises an entrance hall, a bright and welcoming living room, a kitchen/dining area, two well-proportioned bedrooms and a main family bathroom.\n\nThe property sits on a generous site with private gardens surrounding the home, offering ample outdoor space and excellent potential for further enhancement or extension (subject to the relevant planning permission). There is also off-street parking available within the property boundaries.\n\nConveniently located, the property benefits from excellent accessibility with the M9 motorway approximately 1015 minutes away, providing direct routes to Kilkenny City, Carlow, Waterford and Dublin. This makes the property an ideal choice for commuters seeking rural living with strong transport links.\n\nA range of primary and secondary schools are easily accessible, all located within a short drive of the property. Kilkenny City itself offers an excellent range of amenities including shops, restaurants, cafés, sporting facilities, public transport links and cultural attractions such as Kilkenny Castle and St. Canice's Cathedral.\n\nThis charming detached cottage combines countryside tranquillity with convenient access to the city and major transport routes, making it a highly appealing property for a wide range of buyers.\n\nACCOMMODATION\n\nEntrance / Living Area Bright and inviting space featuring tiled flooring, an abundance of natural light, and charming original wooden ceiling beams that add character and warmth, complete with a stove fireplace creating a cosy focal point.\n\nKitchen Fully fitted kitchen with tiled flooring, offering ample under and overhead storage along with integrated appliances for modern convenience.\n\nMain Bathroom Stylishly finished with floor-to-ceiling tiling, complete with a classic white suite and a walk-in shower.\n\nFirst Floor\n\nBedroom 1 Well-proportioned room with wooden flooring and a skylight, ideal as a bedroom or potential home office space.\n\nBedroom 2 Spacious double bedroom featuring wooden flooring and generous proportions.\n\n*Disclaimer - photos have been edited using AI to enhance or brighten the image*"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Ideal for first-time buyers, downsizers, or investors seeking rental potential in a high-demand area.</li><li> Prime location within close proximity to Kilkenny City.</li><li> Excellent access to local amenities including shops, cafés, and schools.</li><li> 10 Minute drive to the M9 linking to Waterford, Carlow & Dublin.</li><li> Oil fired heating.</li><li> Private septic tank & mains water.</ul>"
      },
